# Test: ze show host dmi returns SMBIOS/DMI inventory JSON without a daemon
# VALIDATES: offline fallback -- `show host dmi` runs the in-process
#            host.DetectDMI when no daemon is reachable, producing JSON with
#            the system-vendor field read from /sys/class/dmi/id.
# PREVENTS: regressions where show host dmi silently requires a daemon,
#           or where the DMI JSON drops its canonical kebab-case fields.
# PLATFORM: host inventory reads /sys/class/dmi/id; the darwin detector
# (dmi_other.go) returns ErrUnsupported at build time so the underlying
# feature cannot succeed. Skip on darwin per rules/os-specific-tests.md.
# The system-vendor field requires SMBIOS/DMI to be present (true on the
# QEMU CI host and on bare-metal x86); sys_vendor is world-readable.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp { }
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show host dmi
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="system-vendor"
